Subject: [PATCH] docs(disclosures): PAD-125 value-asserting conformance
 predicates, PAD-126 convention-ambiguity gating

PAD-125 supersedes the presence-based satisfaction predicate of PAD-079 section 3,
which admits null-evidence conformance: a structurally complete but semantically
empty credential set (zero-event safety record, envelope-breach motion digest,
hardware-root label without attestation) satisfies the requirements it was meant
to evidence. Requirements now carry a value assertion, with a dependency form so a
descriptive field cannot stand in for the proof that substantiates it.

PAD-126 discloses gating a physical action proposed by a learned model whose output
semantics are unattested: decide against the conservative envelope over all candidate
interpretations, so the gate may over-deny but cannot under-deny, and bind the
candidate set and assumed interpretation into the signed decision record so historical
decisions can be re-adjudicated once the convention is established.

PAD-079 receives a dated editorial note pointing to PAD-125. Its original text is
unaltered, preserving the integrity of its 2026-07-04 prior-art date.

Signed-off-by: Ramprasad G <groups.rampy1@gmail.com>
