+## August 10, 2026: Conformance Soundness and Model-Semantics Safety (PAD-125 to PAD-126)
+
+Two disclosures arising from hardening the robotics conformance and VLA-gating stack.
+PAD-125 supersedes the presence-based satisfaction predicate of PAD-079 §3: a conformance
+checker that tests whether a credential *carries* a field is satisfied by evidence that is
+structurally complete and semantically empty — a safety record of zero events, a motion
+digest reporting an envelope breach, a hardware-root label with no attestation — and
+certifies it. The corrected predicate asserts the value the clause requires, and the
+failure class ("null-evidence conformance") is named so any credential-based compliance
+scheme can test for it. PAD-126 addresses a distinct hazard: a learned action model's
+output semantics (which element, which units, which direction) are documentation, not
+attestation, so a safety gate converting model output into physical quantities inherits an
+uncheckable assumption whose inverted failure mode points toward *permission*. The gate
+decides against the conservative envelope over all candidate interpretations — so it may
+over-deny but cannot under-deny — and binds the candidate set and assumed interpretation
+into the signed decision record, making historical decisions re-adjudicable once the
+convention is established. Both differentiate against their prior art (schema validation
+and constraint languages; interval arithmetic, robust control, and safety filters) rather
+than claiming the general mechanisms.
 
 
